        "name": "USN-7797-3",
        "description": "Several security issues were discovered in the Linux kernel. An attacker could possibly use these to compromise the system. This update corrects flaws in the following subsystems:   - Virtio block driver;   - Media drivers;   - Network drivers;   - Framebuffer layer;   - BTRFS file system;   - Ext4 file system;   - Network file system (NFS) server daemon;   - Packet sockets;   - VMware vSockets driver; (CVE-2025-38618, CVE-2024-35849, CVE-2025-37785, CVE-2024-49924, CVE-2025-38617, CVE-2024-27078, CVE-2021-47149, CVE-2021-47319, CVE-2025-21796, CVE-2021-47589)",
